The CMS can now collect metrics (JVM, REST API requests, publish process, transactions, sessions, database connection pool and caches) and serve them in the Prometheus format on a separate port. Metrics are disabled by default and are enabled with METRICS_ENABLED; port and interface are set with METRICS_PORT and METRICS_HOST (defaults 8081 and 127.0.0.1). When the CMS runs with the OpenTelemetry Java agent, the CMS specific metrics are additionally sent to the configured OTLP endpoint. The Helm chart has the new settings cms.metrics.enabled and cms.metrics.port.
